 "equipment_type": "Air handler (rack-mounted room cooling unit, split DX)",
 "applies_to": "Schneider Electric Uniflair Rack Mounted Room Cooling units ACRMD4Kxxx (indoor rack unit with matching outdoor unit), register map part number 990-91589.",
 "summary": "The Uniflair ACRMD4K is a rack-mounted split DX cooling unit (indoor unit plus outdoor unit). Its controller is a Modbus RTU / TCP slave. This map covers the unit on/off coil, alarm and output status bits (including outdoor-unit compressor and inverter faults), return and outlet air temperatures, return humidity, pressures, compressor frequency, coil temperatures, operating mode and the writable temperature, humidity, alarm and fan-speed settings.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU",
  "TCP"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "Modicon",
  "note": "Each row shows a Modicon number (00001 / 10002 / 30002 / 40101 style), a hex and a decimal absolute register. The notes say absolute register 0 is Modicon 40001 and address zero on the wire, so the decimal column is the wire address; e.g. holding 40121 is wire 120 and input status 10002 is wire 1."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "Modbus Register Map: Uniflair Rack Mounted Room Cooling ACRMD4Kxxx",
  "doc_number": "990-91589",
  "revision_date": "2022-02",
  "url": "https://download.se.com/files?p_Doc_Ref=Modbus_Register_Map_990-91589",
  "pages": "pp. 1-4 (notes p. 1)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Per the map's notes, 16-bit values are big-endian and signed values are two's complement; all points here are single registers or bits.",
  "Scale: the map's 'Units' column holds the resolution (e.g. 0.1 °C, 0.1 %) and the row text says values are 'magnified 10 times' (219 = 21.9). The map's 'Scale' column actually holds the raw setting range; ranges are given in the descriptions.",
  "Air return humidity (30014) and the discharge/suction pressures (30037, 30038) are printed with the unit '0.1 °C', which looks copied from the temperature rows. We keep the 0.1 scale but leave the unit blank because the map does not give the real unit.",
  "Holding register 40183 (wire 182) carries two settings as bits: bit 10 = PTC heater function, bit 11 = condensation pump function (0 = yes, 1 = no).",
  "Reads use function code 3 or 4; writes use function code 16, or 6 for single registers. The general notes name only these function codes, but the tables also list one coil and input-status points.",
  "The map prints no revision or date; 2022-02 is the PDF's own creation date (2022-02-10)."
 ],
